You'll probably see something like:

drwx------ bilal-ahmed bilal-ahmed /home/bilal-ahmed

The ------ for others means user1 cannot enter your home directory.

2. Check permissions

Run:

ls -ld /home/bilal-ahmed

You'll probably see something like:

drwx------ bilal-ahmed bilal-ahmed /home/bilal-ahmed

The ------ for others means user1 cannot enter your home directory.

3. For this lab, give others access to your home directory

Run:

sudo chmod 755 /home/bilal-ahmed

This gives:

owner  → rwx
group  → r-x
others → r-x

4. Make sure sticky-lab is still 777
chmod 777 /home/bilal-ahmed/sticky-lab

Check:

ls -ld /home/bilal-ahmed/sticky-lab

You should see:

drwxrwxrwx ... sticky-lab

5. Login as user1 again

